WEBVTT

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.608
Ume-dono?

00:01:44.208 --> 00:01:46.280
You’re leaving the Five Leaves?

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.860
Yeah. I’m washing my hands of them.

00:01:49.768 --> 00:01:51.208
I see.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.220
Despite that, you are wondering about our next job, right?

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:00.140
Like “has everything been checked out?”

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.840
Right, Matsu?

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:11.080
If you are leaving, we can no longer gather here.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:17.380
In that case, I will only show myself at Ichi’s place.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.780
Yes, don’t come at all!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.640
I’ll go to Ichi-san’s place to inform him about our next objective.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.428
You’ll get the details from him.

00:02:31.428 --> 00:02:32.688
Okay.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:38.960
What are you doing, Okinu?

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.520
I’ve already cut the brined vegetables.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.680
Since Matsu-san won’t be coming anymore, I thought I’d wrap this for him.

00:02:49.428 --> 00:02:52.648
Leave it be. He’ll be coming again, anyway.

00:02:52.648 --> 00:02:56.728
If Matsu-san said he won’t come, then that means he won’t come.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:03.068
Even you believed him, Daddy,
by telling him not to come at all.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:10.880
Take that and give it to him, Masa. The guy’s quick on his feet.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.648
Matsukichi-dono.

00:03:34.768 --> 00:03:38.440
I got lost, so it took me a while to get here.

00:03:39.388 --> 00:03:42.488
Here. These are brined vegetables from Okinu-dono.

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:44.268
Leave ’em there.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.668
That is beautiful.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.268
Don’t touch.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.120
It’s for sale.

00:03:58.148 --> 00:04:03.040
If I sent this to my little sister back home, she would be delighted.

00:04:06.468 --> 00:04:08.348
What time is it now?

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.328
Let’s see... It is around eight.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.928
How long do you plan to stay?

00:04:21.948 --> 00:04:23.788
Forgive my rudeness.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.928
He took the money with him.

00:04:40.108 --> 00:04:46.448
It seems his circumstances cannot be solved with just the money he gets from being a jeweler.

00:04:47.168 --> 00:04:48.480
What was that?

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.180
You mean what I just said?

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.740
It was hard to hear.

00:05:04.808 --> 00:05:08.948
So... Didn’t you say you were attending a dojo?

00:05:11.068 --> 00:05:13.040
The dojo?

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:21.500
That vassal named Yagi...
Do you know a lot about him?

00:05:22.168 --> 00:05:25.448
Well, that man is hard to understand,

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:28.928
even if he is good with a sword.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.800
But his discernment is keen.

00:05:34.768 --> 00:05:36.460
When will you meet him next?

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.648
He seems busy as of late.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.928
There’s something curious about that man.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:52.048
Did something happen?

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:56.768
Oh, no. It does not involve you.

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:03.528
I have two benefactors to whom I will forever lower my head.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.508
You are one of them.

00:06:12.648 --> 00:06:14.908
So did something happen?

00:06:16.548 --> 00:06:21.188
TL Note: Kifuda are wooden charms

00:06:16.548 --> 00:06:21.188
I was entrusted with the safekeeping of some kifudas from various fiefdoms.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.560
They’re needed for entry to the daimyo’s mansion,

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.368
but they’re gone.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:30.020
Where were they?

00:06:32.668 --> 00:06:35.868
They were supposed to be inside those drawers.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.208
So they’ve disappeared.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.188
Mm-hmm.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.120
Master.

00:06:46.048 --> 00:06:47.680
It’s Ootsuya-san.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:49.048
Zensuke?

00:06:49.048 --> 00:06:51.060
I saw him.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:53.140
He was already a business rival,

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:57.128
but he became really upset when you received

00:06:57.128 --> 00:07:00.120
the patronage of both the daimyo and the vassal.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:03.228
He came unexpectedly the other day...

00:07:03.228 --> 00:07:04.520
Hi!

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.928
This is a fine scroll.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:13.128
Ootsuya-san was right beside that alcove when you were absent.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:18.380
Even if he took them, Ootsuya-san has no use for those kifuda.

00:07:18.948 --> 00:07:24.208
But he knows your clients will be angered. Then, he will prey on the ones who have lost faith in you.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:29.128
Zensuke. You can’t be telling anyone else about this.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:31.788
Matsukichi-san.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:37.180
This is just our problem. It does not involve you.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:43.700
You are usually level-headed, Matsukichi-san, but you can get extreme at times.

00:08:05.828 --> 00:08:07.140
Anything wrong?

00:08:07.868 --> 00:08:08.808
No.

00:08:09.108 --> 00:08:12.800
This house is so old that it creaks a lot.

00:08:52.048 --> 00:08:55.980
It’s just like Sensei said: It seems we have a rat.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.780
A rat from Kikuya, perhaps?

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:01.008
You’re looking for this, correct?

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:08.648
How detestable of Kikuya to send this rat.

00:09:08.648 --> 00:09:10.108
Will you kill me?

00:09:10.108 --> 00:09:15.840
Nope, I’ll use you to blackmail Kikuya. Let’s toss him in the cellar.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.080
Matsu?

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:25.540
No. He didn’t come.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:30.428
Hmm. He left yesterday saying he would visit you.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:36.300
It’s strange that Matsu would not keep his word.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:39.368
I think I’ll go check at Nagaya.

00:09:39.368 --> 00:09:41.168
Only if he doesn’t come tonight.

00:09:42.028 --> 00:09:43.088
Akitsu!

00:09:44.928 --> 00:09:46.280
Yagi-dono?

00:09:47.908 --> 00:09:50.748
That is the shop with the delicious dumplings.

00:09:52.608 --> 00:09:54.040
Are you busy of late?

00:09:54.348 --> 00:09:56.120
Well, I wouldn’t say that.

00:09:56.588 --> 00:09:58.508
And that yakuza?

00:09:59.588 --> 00:10:01.208
Is he accompanying you?

00:10:02.128 --> 00:10:03.700
His name is Yaichi-dono.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:08.420
Oh, you did mention an acquaintance with that name.

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.108
He has a handsome face.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:14.920
I’m Yagi.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:16.800
He’s from the dojo.

00:10:26.708 --> 00:10:28.128
Yaichi-dono?

00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:29.440
Never mind.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.068
But still...

00:10:31.068 --> 00:10:34.620
It seems you strike up really disparate friendships.

00:11:03.928 --> 00:11:05.488
Is that true?

00:11:05.488 --> 00:11:07.528
It sure is!

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.188
Did you go to Nagaya?

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:25.688
Just now.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:27.448
And?

00:11:27.448 --> 00:11:30.020
He wasn’t there as I feared.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:34.460
And Yaichi-dono seems to have some
urgent business with Matsukichi-dono.

00:11:37.668 --> 00:11:40.188
But I’ll go search for him again.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:42.260
Masa.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.220
I’ll go, too.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.360
Matsu-san?

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:04.168
Yes.

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:07.320
I haven’t seen him since yesterday.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:09.100
Is it urgent?

00:12:10.168 --> 00:12:11.328
No.

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:14.168
Kid.

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:23.920
What business do you have with Matsu?

00:12:24.128 --> 00:12:29.208
The... The master told me to check on him.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:30.888
Master?

00:12:30.888 --> 00:12:35.348
Matsukichi-san is good friends with the master. He comes to visit frequently.

00:12:35.348 --> 00:12:36.788
Including yesterday.

00:12:37.128 --> 00:12:43.068
That reminds me. The day before yesterday, Matsukichi-dono left with some money.

00:12:43.788 --> 00:12:46.168
Kid. Show me to your master.

00:12:51.488 --> 00:12:53.980
So Matsukichi-san has disappeared?

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:01.168
He does have a strange group of friends.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:07.120
Matsukichi-san is doing bad deeds even now?

00:13:08.328 --> 00:13:13.760
We want to ask you what you know about Matsu’s disappearance.

00:13:21.388 --> 00:13:26.008
It seems that a business rival of mine has stolen some specially-made kifudas.

00:13:26.648 --> 00:13:33.888
I was wondering if Matsukichi-san went to Ootsuya-san in order to retrieve them.

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:37.968
That was why I wanted to check on him.

00:13:37.968 --> 00:13:43.040
So that means Matsu was captured by that business rival?

00:13:43.728 --> 00:13:47.788
If Ootsuya-san has made a move, it would have been clear...

00:13:47.788 --> 00:13:50.500
But he’s not going to announce it now.

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:55.428
What’s your story with Matsu?

00:14:00.708 --> 00:14:02.740
I am loaning him money.

00:14:03.768 --> 00:14:07.020
Matsukichi-san has a child.

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:08.648
A child?

00:14:08.648 --> 00:14:13.588
That child has a serious injury. He needed the money for the treatment.

00:14:14.208 --> 00:14:19.080
Every month, I gave him as much as I could conveniently give,

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.460
and he would come back to repay me.

00:14:22.608 --> 00:14:24.600
So that’s why he takes those jobs.

00:14:38.988 --> 00:14:41.320
Did you injure your arm?

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:45.208
And you’d dare go stealing with that body?

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:51.848
May I ask what made you do it?

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.748
Candles

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:19.528
If we came to establish that he’s been captured...

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:23.968
Let’s leave for now.

00:15:26.268 --> 00:15:31.988
Even if Matsu hasn’t been captured, we’re still here searching for him.

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:38.740
Anyway, we have no choice but to see what move Ootsuya will make.

00:15:39.588 --> 00:15:43.160
It pains me to hear that.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.680
You look troubled.

00:15:51.148 --> 00:15:54.160
Should we put the dojo on hold for another day?

00:15:56.128 --> 00:15:59.368
What? Did you fail to get another job?

00:16:04.348 --> 00:16:05.460
A bodyguard!

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:07.348
What?

00:16:07.628 --> 00:16:09.428
Um, it’s nothing.

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:12.368
Are you going to serve as a guard somewhere?

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:15.720
I hope they will let me serve them.

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:19.948
Is there a reason? I’m listening.

00:16:24.728 --> 00:16:26.788
Nothing you can share, huh?

00:16:27.808 --> 00:16:32.688
No... but I do wish to tell someone.

00:16:33.128 --> 00:16:34.768
Try me.

00:16:38.308 --> 00:16:43.660
Ootsuya the candle maker stole Kikuya’s kifudas.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:49.100
So you want to enter Ootsuya’s place to retrieve those kifudas?

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:57.520
A friend has likely entered Ootsuya’s place since we haven’t seen him for three days.

00:16:58.248 --> 00:17:00.608
The kifudas are another matter for now.

00:17:01.568 --> 00:17:06.220
I might not be able to save that man.

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:10.908
Ume-dono!

00:17:11.668 --> 00:17:16.040
I’m going to Ootsuya’s place. As a guard.

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:17.128
Say that again?

00:17:17.128 --> 00:17:22.148
Yagi-dono introduced Ootsuya to an influential vassal.

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:24.948
Wait, Masa.

00:17:24.948 --> 00:17:30.360
We don’t know who this Yagi really is. We should avoid any stupid moves.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:33.388
But if there’s something I can do, I must do it.

00:17:33.388 --> 00:17:34.440
Masa!

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.740
Kikuya’s master did tell us

00:17:41.308 --> 00:17:48.188
if something like that were to happen, Matsu would act so fast he’d ignore everything else.

00:17:50.128 --> 00:17:51.320
Probably.

00:17:52.128 --> 00:17:57.048
I thought you’d be acting more concerned instead of remaining this calm.

00:17:57.828 --> 00:18:02.480
That’s because you’re the one who knows him best.

00:18:03.048 --> 00:18:04.300
And you...

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:09.308
You’ve been worrying about someone you don’t really get along with.

00:18:09.308 --> 00:18:12.288
That’s because he’s a comrade.

00:18:14.188 --> 00:18:15.988
That’s pretty neat, Ume.

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.080
A comrade, huh?

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:22.800
Here’s to us and many more.

00:18:27.328 --> 00:18:30.460
Nope, I can never leave.

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:32.868
Mm-hmm.

00:18:51.708 --> 00:18:53.020
Hey, what’s happening?

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:57.848
He was trying to escape.

00:19:00.608 --> 00:19:02.788
How long are we going to keep him tied up?

00:19:02.788 --> 00:19:06.768
Can’t say. But we should have a plan to shake down Kikuya by now.

00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:08.940
Here.

00:19:10.508 --> 00:19:11.868
Eat.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.080
Leave him alone.

00:19:14.588 --> 00:19:17.940
No point in keeping him here if he’s gonna die.

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:21.300
We’ve kept him here for days. He’s not gonna die.

00:19:21.748 --> 00:19:23.908
He sure looks plenty pissed.

00:19:24.348 --> 00:19:27.088
Hey, new guy. Take watch.

00:19:34.568 --> 00:19:36.368
So you are here.

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:45.980
I made my way in by becoming a guard.

00:19:47.608 --> 00:19:49.828
You should’ve minded your own business.

00:19:50.608 --> 00:19:54.728
You were looking for answers, right? From the master of Kikuya.

00:20:00.828 --> 00:20:07.088
At that time, I was a freelance thief. I had no family.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:10.308
But then I coupled with a woman.

00:20:11.468 --> 00:20:16.300
I didn’t even know I had a kid until she sought my help for an injury.

00:20:17.188 --> 00:20:22.920
Since I haven’t done anything for my kid, I wanted to pay for the medicines at least.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:30.928
That’s when they both came in -
Ichi-san and the master of Kikuya.

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:36.860
Are you in pain?

00:20:37.708 --> 00:20:42.668
I’ll keep watch for a chance to get us out of here quickly. Remain patient.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.828
Now I have three benefactors.

00:21:09.020 --> 00:21:16.220
I’ve got a feeling that something was hidden

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:25.508
in the words you once told me. Those words cross my mind again and again.

00:21:25.508 --> 00:21:33.928
Yet your voice always sounds the same as before.

00:21:33.928 --> 00:21:40.980
Every time I breathe, I wanna hold you in my arms

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:49.908
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:21:50.748 --> 00:21:57.988
Every time I breathe, I just wanna hold you in my arms again

00:21:59.108 --> 00:22:06.808
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:07.468 --> 00:22:15.048
Every day I need you  All the time I'll be there for you

00:22:15.780 --> 00:22:24.160
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:30.108 --> 00:22:33.240
Next time on House of Five Leaves:

00:22:33.788 --> 00:22:35.120
This is Matsukichi.

00:22:35.848 --> 00:22:40.080
I sometimes see various things while sneaking into and quietly searching

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:44.100
the residences of samurai and merchants,

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:46.788
but I don’t tell Ichi-san about them.

00:22:46.788 --> 00:22:48.008
Well then, the next episode’s title is:

00:22:48.008 --> 00:22:49.880
“Coming to Help.”
